[DOCUMENT]
MID: fc253b52984e44dcab1a569b885010b8
TITLE: Domain: motor state machine
OPTIONS:
  ENABLE_MID: True

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: software_requirements.sgra

[REQUIREMENT]
MID: 63c9848a0ae1497196ffa079e428d789
UID: SWR-FSM-001
TITLE: Motor states
STATEMENT: >>>
The motor state machine shall have the states ``IDLE``, ``RUNNING`` and
``FAULT``, and shall start in ``IDLE``.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-002

[REQUIREMENT]
MID: 63d9c7c3142f4532b187eecd33defae5
UID: SWR-FSM-002
TITLE: Start and stop transitions
STATEMENT: >>>
The ``START`` event shall move ``IDLE`` to ``RUNNING``. The ``STOP`` event
shall move ``RUNNING`` to ``IDLE``. Any other event in those states shall leave
the state unchanged, except ``FAULT``.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-002

[REQUIREMENT]
MID: 148239a9d84f437282de2c49b7afc716
UID: SWR-FSM-003
TITLE: Fault entry and acknowledge
STATEMENT: >>>
The ``FAULT`` event shall move every state to ``FAULT``. In ``FAULT``, only
``CLEAR_FAULT`` shall change the state, and it shall move to ``IDLE``.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-005
